The protocols HRP-301 (VERDANT-1), HRP-201, HLV-204-201 (VASCLEAR-2) and NFR-118-201
(NORTHFELL-2), the products lumiravostat (Ostrevia), Vasclarin and teravelin, the sponsors and
all identifiers are fictional. Guidelines and standards (ICH M11, E6(R3), E8(R1), E9(R1), E20,
SPIRIT 2025, Regulation (EU) No 536/2014, the New Drugs and Clinical Trials Rules 2019, 21 CFR 312,
ISO 14155, CDISC USDM) are named for education; the guidance in the app summarises them and is
not their text or regulatory advice. No commercial protocol authoring system is reproduced. The
app is not a validated system and must not hold real study data. Everything stays in the
browser.

Code list values and their NCI Thesaurus C-codes are taken from the ICH M11 technical
specification (Step 4, 19 November 2025) and the NCI Thesaurus. A few USDM terms whose codes the
app does not hold are exported as teaching terms in the app's own code system, and the export
says so. The export checks are modelled on the kinds of rule in the CDISC DDF conformance rule
catalogue; their identifiers are the app's own.

